1
00:00:00,029 --> 00:00:01,769
Welcome to Rez grid Academy.

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:07,130
In this lesson, we will represent
apparatus, crews, and gps devices.

3
00:00:07,619 --> 00:00:11,399
A vehicle name alone does not
tell a dispatcher its type, home

4
00:00:11,399 --> 00:00:14,060
station, crew, or location source.

5
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,639
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:17,639 --> 00:00:19,579
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:24,399
Engine 1 and Rescue 1 are added with their
unit types and assigned to Station 1.

8
00:00:24,969 --> 00:00:28,490
Units let dispatchers send the
right resources and let everyone

9
00:00:28,490 --> 00:00:30,379
see which apparatus is available.

10
00:00:30,789 --> 00:00:34,339
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

11
00:00:34,339 --> 00:00:36,600
scenarios, not default settings.

12
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:37,429
Units.

13
00:00:37,819 --> 00:00:40,750
Your apparatus, vehicles
and response teams.

14
00:00:41,289 --> 00:00:44,379
Add each unit with its type
and home station group.

15
00:00:44,639 --> 00:00:45,410
Unit types.

16
00:00:45,829 --> 00:00:49,110
Categories such as Engine,
Ladder or Ambulance.

17
00:00:49,469 --> 00:00:53,749
Create unit types before adding
units so each unit can be classified.

18
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:55,700
Hardware location tracking.

19
00:00:56,109 --> 00:00:58,949
GPS devices that report unit locations.

20
00:00:59,369 --> 00:01:02,559
Register each tracking device
and link it to its unit.

21
00:01:02,669 --> 00:01:03,450
New Unit.

22
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:06,300
Add an apparatus, vehicle or team.

23
00:01:06,779 --> 00:01:10,839
List your apparatus or response teams
with their types and home stations.

24
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:15,660
Teams that respond only as individuals
can mark this module not applicable.

25
00:01:15,869 --> 00:01:16,810
Unit Staffing.

26
00:01:17,219 --> 00:01:19,050
Assign crew members to units.

27
00:01:19,439 --> 00:01:23,530
List your apparatus or response teams
with their types and home stations.

28
00:01:23,869 --> 00:01:28,329
Teams that respond only as individuals
can mark this module not applicable.

29
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:31,309
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

30
00:01:31,809 --> 00:01:32,410
Step 1.

31
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:35,190
Create Engine and Rescue unit types.

32
00:01:35,599 --> 00:01:36,289
Step 2.

33
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:40,719
Add Engine 1 with its type,
Station 1, and crew roles.

34
00:01:41,089 --> 00:01:41,860
Step 3.

35
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:46,980
Assign the crew and, when used, register
a tracking device against the unit.

36
00:01:47,229 --> 00:01:48,709
Now verify the result.

37
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:53,040
Confirm the unit type, home
station, crew, and status.

38
00:01:53,359 --> 00:01:56,710
For hardware tracking, check
a recent received position and

39
00:01:56,710 --> 00:01:58,210
the stale-position behavior.

40
00:01:58,550 --> 00:02:03,700
A common problem to watch for: An old
GPS position is not a live position.

41
00:02:04,109 --> 00:02:08,470
Crew assignment, reported unit status,
and physical readiness are distinct.

42
00:02:08,619 --> 00:02:10,160
Your practice task is simple.

43
00:02:10,639 --> 00:02:14,239
Create Engine 1 in the demo
department and verify the assigned

44
00:02:14,239 --> 00:02:15,670
crew from the dispatcher view.

45
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:18,200
Measure incomplete unit records.

46
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:22,400
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

47
00:02:22,849 --> 00:02:26,310
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
